            <ArticleTitle>The Wellcome Foundation Lecture, 1994. The fetal origins of adult disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent findings suggest that many human fetuses have to adapt to a limited supply of nutrients and in doing so they permanently change their physiology and metabolism. These 'programmed' changes may be the origins of a number of diseases in later life, including coronary heart disease and the related disorders: stroke, diabetes and hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
